8-21T16:25:19Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/122693","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122693","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122693.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/122693.patch","merged_at":"2026-08-21T16:25:19Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nSmall follow-up to #109737.\r\n\r\n- The `specular_intensity` field caused the `LightmapData` struct to extend to 80 bytes. To bring it back to 64 bytes, we can utilize the padding space that has always been available in the `normal_xform` field.\r\n- The `uses_lightmap_specular` field in element info causes a redundant memory store to be generated by the compiler. To avoid it, we can manually bit shift and OR it into the `uint32_t` rvalue. The generated code becomes the same as before, just without the redundant store.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nN/A.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public",